{
 "name": "sdlc-factory",
 "title": "The software factory",
 "subtitle": "One gated pipeline for every change, whoever starts it, while people set the rules",
 "description": "Work enters from a person, an issue tracker, factory intake, the task list and the harness's own feedback. A supervised session or an autonomous run defines it; one start gate, which checks the spec, the grill pass, the approval and the task's dependencies, admits it to the build. Every task then passes the same judge, review, verify and CI checks; outward writes are journalled, and one with no observed result waits for a person. A person merges the pull request. People set the rules in user-only files. Dashed parts are proposed or outside the harness.",
 "eyebrow": "SDLC · 1 of 4",
